# Upstream's apps/nufi-agent/.gitattributes opens with `* text eol=lf` and
# then names the binary types it knows about (png, jpg, ico, gif, mp4, svg,
# wav, raw). Webfonts are not on that list, so every .woff2 added under this
# fork is treated as text and line-ending-normalised on `git add`: any CRLF
# byte pair inside the compressed stream is silently rewritten to a single
# LF. Eight of the eighteen files in nufi/fonts/ lost 1-3 bytes that way on
# their first commit -- enough to make the font unparseable, with no error
# anywhere until a browser refuses to render it.
#
# This file is scoped to nufi/ (deeper .gitattributes wins) so the fix does
# not mean editing an upstream-owned file. check-brand-css.sh verifies every
# nufi/fonts/*.woff2 still has an intact WOFF2 header, so a regression here
# fails CI rather than shipping broken glyphs.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff  binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
